     Launcher-style chrome, built as a reusable library:
       · horizontal TOP navigation, unlimited categories at runtime
       · weighted CARD GRID (1 or 2 columns per row, any weight)
       · FOOTER status bar + status pills
       · independent draggable overlay panels
       · modals, drawers, tooltips, context menus, command palette
       · ~50 elements, ~30 animation helpers, one RenderStepped connection
       · a built-in SELF-TEST: 119 live checks you can run from a button

     The bundled demo is a PLACEHOLDER with exactly TWO categories
     ("Main" and "Widgets"). It is a showcase, not an application.
     Set CONFIG.Demo = false to load the library on its own.

     NEW IN 5.5  (four bugs reported from a live client)
       · THEME SWITCH left ~68 of ~164 colour sites on the old palette,
         because only paint()-registered objects were repainted. SetTheme
         now walks the whole tree and remaps any colour matching an old
         token to the new one, so nothing can be missed.
       · NOTIFICATION SPAM: a slider or colour-picker drag fires its
         callback every frame. Toasts now coalesce by title (with an xN
         counter) and the stack is hard-capped at Config.NotifyMax.
         ColorPicker gained OnCommit, which fires once on release.
       · SLIDER COULD NOT BE DRAGGED: it read GetMouseLocation(), which is
         inset-adjusted and lags the event. It now reads the input
         object's own Position, has an Active 34px hit area, and clamps.
       · ANIMATIONS: every preset was badly under-damped (Groovy was
         zeta 0.41 = 24% overshoot), so everything wobbled. All routine
         presets are now zeta ~= 0.98 - they land once and stop. Drag
         tilt/wobble and the idle logo pulse / icon rock are OFF by
         default. The Signal meter is gone.

     NEW IN 5.3  (fixes reported from a live client)
       · AddCard passed ScrollingFrame-only properties to a plain Frame.
         Roblox raised "ScrollBarImageColor3 is not a valid member of
         Frame" on the FIRST card, which killed the demo: one nav pill,
         no content, no overlay panels, Entf apparently dead.
       · Dragging rewritten. A Frame with Active = false never receives
         InputBegan, so the title bar was deaf. There is now one Active
         TextButton behind the chrome; Roblox routes button presses away
         from it, so no hit-testing is needed. The old hit-test also read
         .Visible on UICorner, which throws.
       · UIScale has no Rotation property - three chevrons/icons were
         writing it. They now rotate their Frame.
       · Boot failures are reported ON SCREEN instead of dying silently.
       · The test harness now validates every property against the
         official Roblox API dump and applies UIScale to AbsoluteSize,
         so this whole class of bug is caught before delivery.
       · Main rebuilt to match the reference launcher: place banner plus
         two quiet list panels. Card borders softened; far less blue.

     NEW IN 5.2
       · Dragging no longer teleports the window. One spring per property,
         a 4px drag threshold, presses on nav pills ignored, ancestor
         UIScale honoured, focus loss releases the grab, carry capped.
       · Drag wobble is ~4x gentler and tunable via CONFIG.Drag.
       · Aether:SelfTest(win) - 119 checks, runnable in-game from a button.
       · Widgets tab gained a Self-test card and a Motion gallery with a
         button for every single animation.
       · Tab:Destroy, Panel:Destroy, status pill :Destroy, dropdown
         :SetOpen/:Toggle, Motion.Forget/Stop, Spring:SetPreset.
       · Studio's script analysis is clean: no type errors, no unused
         locals, no duplicate function definitions.

     Paste this whole file into ONE LocalScript, or execute it once.
